N/g ↗</span></a></div></section></div>","sourceUrl":"https://vibe-hub.org/en/single-page-layout","markdown":"# Single Page\n\nYou might say\nPut everything on one long page so people can just scroll through it.\n\n**Arrange a complete story in sections down one scrolling page**·A single-page layout guides visitors through a sequence such as value, proof, features, pricing, and action. It works when the story has one main goal. Clear sections and anchor navigation help, but important content should not depend on scroll effects.\nKnow first\n[Navbar](/vibe-hub/navbar?lang=en)[Hero](/vibe-hub/hero?lang=en)[CTA](/vibe-hub/cta?lang=en)[Footer](/vibe-hub/footer?lang=en)\n\nSingle Page Layout\n\n## You can say this to an AI Agent\n\n> “\n> Organize the landing page as one scrolling sequence: problem, value, product evidence, customer proof, and CTA. Give sections stable anchors and long-page return paths, and repeat the same primary action only at useful decision stages.\n\n### When to use it\n\n- Product landing page\n\nProduct featuresPricingCustomer reviewsFAQ\n- Campaign page\n\nCore valueKey benefitsNext\n- Portfolio story\n\nCore value→Key benefits→Credible evidence→Next\n- A focused site with one main conversion goal\n\nInstallQuick startAPIFAQ\nScroll to “Quick start” and the table of contents highlights it automatically\n\n### When NOT to use it\n\n- Force a large multi-purpose product into one endless page\n\nThe long page lacks anchors and a back-to-top entry point.\n- Hide content behind complex scroll animation\n\nValueBenefitsEvidencePricingFAQNext\n- Repeat the same action after every short paragraph\n\n🔍 Search usernamesCreate user\n\nAlex ChenAdmin\n\nMaya LeeMembers\n- Use sections with no clear narrative order\n\nValueBenefitsBenefitsNext\n\nAnatomy\n\nCore ValueMain AdvantagesCredible EvidenceCall to Action\n\n1HeroExplain who the product is for, what problem it solves, and provide clear next steps\n\n2FeaturesOrganize key capabilities by user tasks to avoid too much information at the same level\n\n3ProofUse authorized, verifiable cases, data or reviews to support claims\n\n4CTAProvide clear next steps at appropriate reading points\n\nVariants\n\nAnchors\n\nThere are many paragraphs and you need to jump at any time\n\nPure Scroll\n\nA small landing page finished in three or four screens\n\nBackTop\n\n↑\n\nThe page is long and a quick entry to return to the top needs to be provided.\n\nTypical use cases\n\nProduct launch\n\nTurn meeting recordings into editable notes\n\n        \nUpload a recording to draft a transcript, summary, and action items\n\n        Try the demo\n\n      \n🎙️\n\nTranscription\n\nEditable draft\n\n        \n🤖\n\nSummary\n\nKey points and action items\n\n        \n📤\n\nSharing\n\nShare with a link\n\n      \nBuilt for collaborative review\n        Get started\n\nPersonal portfolio\n\nJuly 26 · Shenzhen · In person\n        \nHands-on Vibe Coding Workshop\n\n        \nBeginner-friendly—bring your laptop and leave with a working project\n\n      \n**14:00**Build your first page\n\n        \n**15:30**Take a prototype through deployment\n\n      \nSmall-group workshop · Registration required\n        Register\n\nEvent page\n\nDo difficult things with interesting people\n\n        \nRemote friendly\n          Option incentives\n          Mac standard\n\n      \nSenior front-end engineer\n\nBeijing · Full-time · 30-50K\n\n          Delivery\n\n        \nAI Product Manager\n\nShanghai · Full-time · 25-45K\n\n          Delivery\n\nCampaign landing page\n\nAli\n\n        \nIndependent developers · Use AI to make small and beautiful tools\n\n      \n📝 My blog · Weekly updates\n\n        \n🚀 Products in progress · Miaojian App\n\nRecommended tool\n[Web fine-tuning tool · Selector Pro\n\n## Select page elements for precise AI edits\n\nClick a button, text, or card, note the change, then copy its exact location to AI.\nOpen Selector Pro website↗\n\nyour-site.com\n\n**Button · Get started**Use a smaller r